[length:04:16]
[ti:Aracnephobia - I brought myself back home]
[ar:Aracnephobia]
[al:Chaotic-Dysfuntional]
[au:Aracne]
[lr:Aracne]
[re:LRC Workbench by Azaria (lrc-workbench.azariadev.dev)]
[ve:0.3.3]
[00:03.06]There was a kingdom 
[00:05.09]in the bath.
[00:07.29]A beam of light.
[00:09.86]A little spell to grow.
[00:12.51]You closed your eyes.
[00:15.52]You believed him.
[00:19.81]AND
[00:20.58]NOW
[00:21.17]LOOK AT ME
[00:31.60]I came a long way back
[00:33.46]to find that little girl
[00:35.93]WHO LEFT THE FUCKING DOOR UNLOCKED
[00:38.17]AND TRUSTED IN THE WORLD.
[00:40.88]The one who drew the pictures
[00:43.04]while he created worlds.
[00:45.63]The one who learned that love
[00:47.21]meant being understood.
[00:50.00]So every time they showed their teeth,
[00:52.67]you waited for those frozen eyes
[00:56.38]to remind you
[00:59.85]You 
[01:00.54]deserve 
[01:01.29]to be 
[01:01.89]loved.
[01:03.11]I can hold two things
[01:05.44]without choosing one.
[01:07.49]My big grey eyes can still shine
[01:09.94]while they cry for what they lost.
[01:12.11]My legs can shake beneath me
[01:14.28]while I find my way back home.
[01:16.67]One foot covered in fairy dust.
[01:18.96]One foot tied to pain.
[01:20.66]If nobody comes for me,
[01:23.01]I can still go home
[01:25.70]ALONE.
[01:30.46]...alone
[01:35.76]You don't know what I know.
[01:38.35]Fairy rings
[01:39.45]RUST.
[01:40.12]Magical worlds
[01:41.48]don't work with bath salts.
[01:44.06]There was a cliff.
[01:45.52]We slipped.
[01:46.65]You waited.
[01:47.87]No hand reached down for us.
[01:49.22]No miracle.
[01:50.15]No incantation.
[01:51.70]Your little fingers found the earth.
[01:54.14]YOU CLIMBED BACK UP ALONE.
[01:57.51]Remember that.
[01:59.18]Because it will happen every time.
[02:11.41]There is no such thing as eternal love.
[02:15.00]The compass does not always point north.
[02:19.69]The one who taught you
[02:21.22]to believe in yourself
[02:22.55]becomes the one
[02:23.58]who makes you doubt everything.
[02:25.74]The safest hands.
[02:27.36]The coldest eyes.
[02:28.99]The man you'd give your life for
[02:31.52]Let you fall
[02:32.71]TWICE.
[02:39.00]-Are we still drawing?
[02:40.20]-...Yes.
[02:41.00]-And are we still singing?
[02:42.40]-Better than ever.
[02:43.61]-Then what did I do wrong
[02:45.39]-Nothing.
[02:47.51]I can hold two things
[02:49.73]without choosing one.
[02:51.90]My big grey eyes can still shine
[02:54.16]while they cry for what they lost.
[02:56.43]My legs can shake beneath me
[02:58.43]while I find my way back home.
[03:00.70]One foot covered in fairy dust.
[03:03.06]One foot tied to pain.
[03:04.69]Nobody came for me.
[03:08.71]I still found my way back 
[03:12.18]HOME
[03:16.37]...alone.
[03:21.86]Pour the child into the woman.
[03:26.38]Pour the woman into the dream.
[03:30.42]I can know the truth
[03:32.29]and keep the wonder.
[03:34.87]I can lose my north
[03:36.61]and still move forward.
[03:40.16]I can hold two things.
[03:43.54]I can hold…
[03:46.35]myself.
[03:51.54]myself.
[03:57.07]There was a kingdom in the bath.
[04:00.33]It wasn't magic.
[04:02.79]But it was real.
[04:06.94]The cat's tongue chocolate...
[04:08.61]was always betrayal.
